32] == 0` (past the end of `.data`) and\n`cp_len_extra_bits[31] == 0` (an alignment gap).\"\"\"\nassert old2 in s\ns = s.replace(old2, new2)\n\ns += \"\"\"\n\n## Differential verification (this repository)\n\nRun everything with:\n\n```sh\ncd translation && ./verify.sh\n```\n\nwhich builds the C reference exactly as the task specifies, builds the Rust\n`cdylib`, diffs `nm -D`, and runs all four test binaries under every cargo\nfeature combination.  See `SYMBOLS.md`, `CONFIGS.md` and `ERRORS.md` for the\nphase artifacts and results.\n\nThe tests **never link the Rust crate**: it is a `cdylib` only, and\n`tests/common/mod.rs` loads *both* `.so`s with `libloading` (`dlopen`/`dlsym`),\nso every call exercises the `#[no_mangle] extern \"C\"` exports the way an external\nconsumer would.\n\n| file | what it does |\n|---|---|\n| `tests/common/mod.rs` | harness: dual `dlopen`, PNG/zlib/DEFLATE builders (CRC32, adler32, canonical Huffman, stored / fixed / dynamic block emitters), seeded RNG, corpus writer, and the classifier |\n| `examples/diffrunner.rs` | replays a corpus against **one** library, each record in a forked child, printing one deterministic line per record; run once per library and the stdouts are compared byte for byte |\n| `tests/phase_b_valid.rs` | 49 tests, one per `CONFIGS.md` row (valid inputs) |\n| `tests/phase_c_errors.rs` | 29 tests, one per `ERRORS.md` row, plus generic boundaries and fuzz corpora |\n| `tests/phase_d_symbols.rs` | 5 tests: symbol parity, sizes, `RTLD_NOW` load, `.data` layout |\n\nThree things the harness has to do to make the comparison meaningful, all of\nwhich are consequences of the C's own undefined behaviour:\n\n1. **Forked children.** The reference build has `assert()` **enabled**\n   (`CMakeLists.txt` sets no `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`), so many malformed inputs abort\n   it; others segfault.  Each record therefore runs in a forked child\n   (`PR_SET_DUMPABLE 0` so the kernel does not hand 800 core dumps to\n   systemd-coredump) with a