{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_rctxq56smepyvellzc332ssuuwlplxq4j2jdgz55waajzncnfz6a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — all four phases pass. **Two real divergences were found and fixed.**\n\n## Bugs found & fixed\n\n1. **`.data` layout of the exported tables (real behavioural bug).** `cp_block` indexes `cp_len_extra_bits[symbol-257]` / `cp_len_base` / `cp_dist_*` with values up to 4095 when a corrupt Huffman tree is decoded, so the C reads *past* a table into the next one. `src/lib.rs` modelled the **reverse** (`-O1+`) table order; the reference build (`-O0`, per the documented cmake command) uses **source** order. Every out-of-range read returned the wrong byte — e.g. `cp_len_extra_bits[32]`: C reads `cp_len_base[0]`'s LSB = 3, the model returned 16. Fixed in `blob_byte()`, now pinned by `phase_d_symbols::c_data_layout_is_source_order`.\n\n2. **Profile under test.** A *debug* Rust build turns the C's NULL deref in `cp_inflate(NULL, 8, out, 1)` into a panic/abort (`core`'s debug assertions in `ptr::read_unaligned`) where C takes SIGSEGV. The release build (what the crate declares, `panic = \"abort\"`) segfaults identically; the harness now loads that.\n\n## Artifacts (crate root)\n\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — 9/9 C symbols exported by Rust, same types and OBJECT sizes; 0 unresolved imports (`dlopen(RTLD_NOW)` check).\n- `ERRORS.md` — 34 rejection rows + 10 `assert` rows + 13 generic boundaries, all checked.\n- `CONFIGS.md` — 50 valid-input configuration rows, all checked.\n\n## Tests (87, all passing, all through `libloading` on both `.so`s)\n\n`phase_b_valid.rs` (49) · `phase_c_errors.rs` (29) · `phase_d_symbols.rs` (5) · lib unit tests (4). `./verify.sh` runs the whole thing for `<default>` and `<no-default-features>` (Cargo.toml declares no features).\n\nThree harness details were necessary because of the C's own UB, and each surfaced a class of false positive I had to eliminate rather than paper over:\n- The reference build has `assert()` **enabled**, so ~800 malformed inputs abort it. Each record runs in a forked child; on `SIGABRT` the Rust result is compared against a second `gcc -O0 -DNDEBUG` build (identical `.data` layout).\n- `load_png_mem` hashes uninitialised `malloc` memory for short streams. The runner primes the allocator's free lists with a known byte; running each library under two different bytes isolates exactly the heap-dependent records (2–37 per corpus) instead of letting them read as translation bugs.\n- With `NDEBUG` the C can loop forever (zero-bit, zero-length match consumes no bits), so children get a 1 s alarm — and the harness still *fails* if the Rust loops where the C terminates.\n\n`c_src/` is untouched apart from the `build/` directory cmake created."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":579,"cache_read_input_tokens":314193,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":579,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1fcac8c8-de4d-4f5d-bb4e-dc7d70d6fb9c","uuid":"e28a8b47-4982-471a-8471-68b41f7750f1","timestamp":"2026-09-05T10:33:11.511Z"}
